| explorer | hit | Explorer digest this session: no run key or cache (`run.py:1144`), tool results discarded (`parse.py:10-16`), instructions compiled in (`src/mcp/mod.rs:76`, `definitions.rs:4,10,117`), byte-lock and AGENTS.md lockstep tests (`mod.rs:771-803`, `mod.rs:1231`), power gate (`PHASE4_PLAN.md:3-25`); FeatureBench research at `8d4e347` (agent in container, separable `fb eval`, `/root/my_repo` leak, 10–19 GB images, GPU flags) |

## Approach

Build a result substrate first, then two independent adapters, then the panel, then the loop.

1. **Result substrate (G-4, G-5, F-6).** Every row gains a `run_key`, the agent CLI version, the timeout, and a pointer to an untruncated trajectory sidecar holding every tool call with its input and output. A baseline store returns an existing row for a matching key instead of calling a model. `run.py` gains a required `--max-usd` ceiling on paid runs, summed from native cost. `PHASE4_PLAN.md` is marked superseded by this spec (F-6).
2. **FeatureBench adapter (F-1, G-1).** Our runner starts the agent inside a container from the digest-pinned per-repo image, reproduces the native Level 1 setup exactly (copy, mask patch, F2P test deletion, `/root/my_repo` deletion, git init), runs the claude or codex CLI with the candidate tilth binary mounted, and extracts `git diff --cached` as the patch. The pinned upstream `fb eval` grades it in a fresh container. A task enters a panel only after gold, empty, and tampered patches grade correctly on this host. Dataset v1.1 and grader `8d4e347` are pinned.
3. **Model judge (F-5, G-6).** A pinned judge labels each panel task once for structural-tool applicability from its problem statement and gold patch, cached by task, dataset revision, judge model, and prompt hash. It critiques each rollout from its trajectory. Both outputs are gated by agreement with a hand-labeled calibration set. Critiques feed reflection only; they never enter a score.
4. **Panel manifest (G-2, G-3).** A pre-registered panel lists the admitted FeatureBench tasks, `gin_edit_render_context`, and the cherry-picks `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, `gin_servehttp_flow`, with a stratified dev/test split committed before the first paid run.
5. **Evolution loop (F-2, F-3, F-4).** GEPA `optimize_anything` evolves candidates; each candidate is materialized as a commit on a scratch branch (F-2). A mutation may touch any of `src/**` and `prompts/**` except evaluator paths (F-4); the applier then regenerates `AGENTS.md` and updates the byte lock mechanically. Each candidate runs an evaluator cascade: cargo build, test, and clippy; `tests/mcp_v2` when `src/edit/**` changed; the cheap tier; then the paid tier against frozen baseline rows (F-3, G-5). The score is grader correctness only; trajectories and judge critiques are reflection side information (F-5). Frontier candidates are re-run before acceptance (F-3). At the end, the best frontier candidates are scored once on the held-out test split and the winner opens as a draft PR (F-4).

## Decisions

- F-1: FeatureBench runs through our runner with the agent inside the task container and the pinned upstream `fb eval` grader in a fresh container — keeps rows in our JSONL and avoids grading in the agent-touched container.
- F-2: One evolutionary loop mutates code and text; a candidate is a commit — instructions are compiled in, and `variant.git_sha` / `binary_sha256` already prove what was served.
- F-3: The loop engine is GEPA `optimize_anything` with repeat runs on frontier candidates — trajectory reflection matches G-4 and it has the best measured budget (150–600 metric calls).
- F-4: The loop may mutate all of `src/**` and `prompts/**` except evaluator paths; winners land as human-reviewed draft PRs — user chose the widest search space; the cascade is the backstop.
- F-5: The judge labels per-task applicability and critiques each rollout for reflection only; grader correctness is the only objective — the loop cannot game a score it cannot touch.
- F-6: The Phase 4 power gate is retired; every paid run requires an explicit dollar ceiling — user retired the gate; `--max-usd` replaces it as the spend control.
- _Minor decisions:_ cherry-picks are existing hard tasks (also the cheap tier); dataset v1.1 + grader `8d4e347`; CPU-only Level 1 panel; `src/edit/**` mutations also gate on `tests/mcp_v2`; diffs inside `#[cfg(test)]` spans are rejected except the applier's byte-lock update; the judge model is pinned and recorded in the run key; `--max-usd` has no default.

## Acceptance

- AC-1: WHEN `run.py` runs a FeatureBench cell THE SYSTEM SHALL start the agent inside a container from the digest-pinned image, apply the native Level 1 setup including deletion of the F2P test file and `/root/my_repo`, and record `git diff --cached` as the cell's patch.  (F-1, G-1)
- AC-2: WHEN a FeatureBench cell finishes THE SYSTEM SHALL grade its patch with the pinned `fb eval` in a fresh container and write `correct` from `resolved`, plus `pass_rate` and F2P/P2P counts, into the row.  (F-1, G-1)
- AC-3: WHEN a FeatureBench task is admitted to a panel THE SYSTEM SHALL require that its gold patch resolves and its empty and tampered patches do not resolve on this host, and SHALL refuse GPU-flagged and Level 2 tasks.  (F-1, G-1)
- AC-4: WHEN a panel manifest is loaded THE SYSTEM SHALL list the admitted FeatureBench tasks, `gin_edit_render_context`, `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, and `gin_servehttp_flow` with a dev/test split, and SHALL refuse a paid run against a manifest whose split changed after its first recorded result.  (G-2, G-3)
- AC-5: WHEN any cell completes THE SYSTEM SHALL write an untruncated trajectory sidecar with every tool call's input and output, and the row SHALL carry `run_key`, `cli_version`, `timeout_s`, and the candidate `git_sha` and `binary_sha256`.  (G-4, F-2)
- AC-6: WHEN a baseline-arm cell is requested and the baseline store holds a row with the same run key THE SYSTEM SHALL reuse that row without a model call, and WHEN no row matches THE SYSTEM SHALL run the cell and store it.  (G-5, F-3)
- AC-7: WHEN a paid run starts without `--max-usd` THE SYSTEM SHALL exit before any model call, and WHEN cumulative native cost plus the next cell's estimate exceeds the ceiling THE SYSTEM SHALL stop before that cell.  (F-6)
- AC-8: WHEN a panel task lacks a cached applicability label for its run key THE SYSTEM SHALL produce one from the problem statement and gold patch with the pinned judge and cache it by task, dataset revision, judge model, and judge prompt hash.  (F-5, G-6)
- AC-9: WHEN the judge's agreement with the hand-labeled calibration set is below the configured threshold THE SYSTEM SHALL refuse to supply labels or critiques to an optimizer run.  (F-5, G-6)
- AC-10: WHEN the optimizer scores a candidate THE SYSTEM SHALL use grader correctness as the only score and pass trajectories and judge critiques only as reflection side information.  (F-5, F-3, G-4)
- AC-11: WHEN the optimizer proposes a candidate THE SYSTEM SHALL materialize it as a commit on a scratch branch, reject any diff touching `benchmark/**`, `tests/**`, `.github/**`, the `Cargo.toml` version line, or a `#[cfg(test)]` span, and then regenerate `AGENTS.md` and the byte lock mechanically.  (F-2, F-4)
- AC-12: WHEN a candidate commit exists THE SYSTEM SHALL evaluate it through the cascade of cargo build, test, and clippy; `tests/mcp_v2` when `src/edit/**` changed; the cheap tier; then the paid tier, and SHALL stop at the first failing stage with score 0 and that stage recorded.  (F-3, F-4)
- AC-13: WHEN a candidate reaches the paid tier THE SYSTEM SHALL compare it against frozen baseline rows without re-running baseline arms, and SHALL re-run a frontier candidate the configured number of times before accepting it onto the frontier.  (F-3, G-5)
- AC-14: WHEN the optimizer run ends THE SYSTEM SHALL score the best frontier candidates once on the held-out test split and open the winner as a draft PR without merging it.  (F-4, F-2)

