## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + NEW SLICE benchmark/featurebench/, benchmark/judge/, benchmark/evolve/
spine step:       workflow (run.py cell loop) + infra (container runner, baseline store)
public interface: featurebench.FeatureBenchTask(Task).prepare_container(image_digest) / extract_patch() / check_correctness()  (F-1)
public interface: featurebench.grade(predictions, *, grader_pin, data_rev) -> list[FbReport]  (F-1)
public interface: featurebench.preflight(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict  (F-1)
public interface: baselines.run_key(cell) -> str; baselines.lookup(key) -> Row | None; baselines.store(row)  (F-3)
public interface: run.py --panel PATH --max-usd FLOAT --candidate-sha SHA  (F-6, F-2)
public interface: panels.load_panel(path) -> Panel(dev, test)  (F-1)
public interface: judge.applicability(task) -> Label; judge.critique(row, trajectory) -> str; judge.calibrate(labels) -> Agreement  (F-5)
public interface: evolve.main(--panel, --max-usd, --max-metric-calls, --seed-sha); evolve.materialize(candidate) -> sha; evolve.cascade(sha) -> (score, side_info); evolve.finish(frontier)  (F-2, F-3, F-4)
private:          docker lifecycle and image digest pinning; native Level 1 setup replay; trajectory sidecar format; judge prompts; GEPA engine config; mutation path allowlist; AGENTS.md regen + byte-lock update
crust delta:      new run.py flags (--panel, --max-usd, --candidate-sha); new row fields (run_key, cli_version, timeout_s, trajectory_path, pass_rate); new packages featurebench/judge/evolve; PHASE4_PLAN.md superseded
arrows:           run.py -> featurebench, baselines, panels; evolve -> run.py, baselines, judge, panels; judge -> baselines (row + sidecar read); no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Risks

- FeatureBench images are 10–19 GB each (~167 GB for Lite); disk and pull time bound which hosts can run the panel.
- GPU-flagged tasks may shrink the CPU-only panel well below 12; admission may yield fewer FeatureBench tasks than hoped.
- Per-instance Pareto selection chases noise on $3–10 rollouts; frontier re-runs cost extra budget.
- Mutating all of `src/` invites overfitting to a ~10-task dev split and quiet weakening of edit safety; the cascade and held-out test split are the only guards.
- Retiring the power gate removes the statistical stop; `--max-usd` limits spend but not false-positive conclusions.
- The `fb eval` pin may disagree with dataset v1.1 environment fixes (mlflow); preflight must catch it.
- Running the claude CLI inside third-party images needs credentials copied in; the wiki records revoked tokens invalidating a whole run.

## Open questions

- [TBD] Candidate representation for `optimize_anything` when the whole `src/` is mutable: a unified diff as one text component, or a custom proposer that runs a coding agent in a worktree. Resolve with a prototype cycle as the first step of the evolution loop curd.
- [TBD] Judge agreement threshold and calibration-set size (default proposal: every panel task for applicability plus 20 trajectories, Cohen's kappa ≥ 0.6).
- [TBD] Frontier re-run count and plateau window (default proposal: 3 re-runs; stop after 5 rounds without dev improvement).

## Quality gates

- `just check`: exits 0 (fmt, clippy, cargo test, `tests/mcp_v2`, `tests/scripts`, bash-guard self-test).
- `cd benchmark && python3 -m pytest tests`: exits 0, including the new `test_featurebench.py`, `test_panels.py`, `test_baselines.py`, `test_judge.py`, `test_evolve.py`.
- `python3 benchmark/featurebench/preflight.py --panel benchmark/panels/<name>.json`: every admitted task reports gold resolved, empty and tampered unresolved.

## Curds

- **c1-result-substrate** — run key, untruncated trajectory sidecar, `cli_version`/`timeout_s` fields, baseline store, `--max-usd`, PHASE4_PLAN superseded. Covers G-4, G-5. ACs 5, 6, 7. Depends on: none. State: proposed.
- **c2-featurebench-adapter** — container runner, native setup replay, patch extraction, pinned `fb eval` grading, preflight. Covers G-1. ACs 1, 2, 3. Depends on: c1. State: proposed.
- **c4-model-judge** — applicability labels, rollout critiques, calibration gate. Covers G-6. ACs 8, 9. Depends on: c1. State: proposed.
- **c3-panel-manifest** — pre-registered panel with Gin, cherry-picks, admitted FeatureBench tasks, and the split lock. Covers G-2, G-3. AC 4. Depends on: c2. State: proposed.
- **c5-evolution-loop** — candidate materialization, mutation allowlist, cascade, GEPA engine, frontier re-runs, held-out scoring, draft PR. Covers G-4, G-5. ACs 10–14. Depends on: c1, c3, c4. State: proposed.

